[[:db/retract 17592186129540 :question/answer-fields 17592186126737] [:db/retract 17592186129539 :question/answer-fields 17592186126731] [:db/retract 17592186129541 :question/answer-fields 17592186126743] [:db/retract 17592186129543 :question/answer-fields 17592186126755] {:db/id 17592186129294 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-3ec15158-435a-5888-95f3-44340c0036cb" "question-1eab4807-9d88-5a37-9ff9-fc1404b92d43" "question-c47fff30-dc4f-5860-a5ab-d77dfee6da24" "question-77273bb6-e09c-5d72-b951-ab16051ede43" "question-47a5c5c7-d82d-5d72-883d-d0468b52660c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129291 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b9628c5b-7fa0-5045-9ac2-ad280b61b082" "question-66bc40ec-8b7f-5a7f-a822-c2240ee2d9f5" "question-d3c48087-507b-57b2-8663-35cf3ca6e4b3"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129292 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-cd5d39c2-8301-5260-adfd-2e9f69bcfb7d" "question-26263261-ed01-57e5-8398-ad944dae02a2" "question-c57b76e6-1edf-5c3c-98a4-e16cf256a5f1" "question-7ff6628f-789d-5102-a51c-36a2bdf1a544"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129293 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b1025740-1de0-548c-b755-7aea427a0e9c" "question-a4435932-14e7-5d5c-ae2a-cc6b7883581b" "question-e7aab632-bc8c-5d87-8d6b-6366b876ba3c" "question-71003ac4-a6c7-5375-9693-7a03dcbed8fa"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-3ec15158-435a-5888-95f3-44340c0036cb" :question/id #uuid "3ec15158-435a-5888-95f3-44340c0036cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-163798" :question/problem "![](images/a4/a4f6cf6f453399ec8b823a447bfb93b1b33668004c22c15dc5b42c413f6226bb.png)\n\nTwo point masses $A$ and $B$ of mass $9\\,kg$ and $3\\,kg$, respectively, are connected by a rigid, massless rod of length $4\\,m$ that is perfectly balanced on a fulcrum, as shown above. Find the distance between the fulcrum and $B.$" :question/worked-solution "Let ${d}_{1}$ and ${d}_{2}$ be the distances between the fulcrum and $A$ and $B$, respectively, as shown below.\n\n![](images/b3/b3650c27d30a72df4d92b4eed8f4cfff71d598b1821d0541632b38722d854210.png)\n\nLet's write down the moment of each mass about the fulcrum:\n\n- The moment of mass $A$ equals $-9\\cdot {d}_{1}=-9{d}_{1}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}$ (negative since the motion induced by this mass would be counterclockwise).\n\n- The moment of mass $B$ equals $3\\cdot {d}_{2}=3{d}_{2}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}$ (positive since the motion induced by this mass would be clockwise).\n\nThe principle of moments tells us that for the two masses to balance perfectly, the sum of the moments must equal zero.\n\nSo, in this case, we have\n\n$$\n3{d}_{2}-9{d}_{1}=0.\n$$\n\nWe need to find ${d}_{2},$ so we eliminate ${d}_{1}.$\nUsing the fact that the rod has length $4\\,m,$ we have\n\n$$\n{d}_{1}+{d}_{2}=4\\,⟹\\,{d}_{1}=4-{d}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{d}_{2}-9(4-{d}_{2}) & =0 \\\\ 3{d}_{2}-36+9{d}_{2} & =0 \\\\ 12{d}_{2} & =36 \\\\ {d}_{2} & =3\\,m.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4040afc8-2ef9-5d9c-b27d-a275e17cb35a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4040afc8-2ef9-5d9c-b27d-a275e17cb35a" :answer-field/id #uuid "4040afc8-2ef9-5d9c-b27d-a275e17cb35a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5aaac2d6-73c4-586e-b4eb-5b146e7bc4a7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b22b22af-5143-5629-8416-48c060ebbe09" "answer-b1c1e3f2-9f26-5edd-a5f3-733721f9597a" "answer-5aaac2d6-73c4-586e-b4eb-5b146e7bc4a7" "answer-d3d50606-3008-5ec2-9486-4aa0714bad59" "answer-c378fc4c-4720-5991-98f2-269c5c81ef42"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b22b22af-5143-5629-8416-48c060ebbe09" :answer/id #uuid "b22b22af-5143-5629-8416-48c060ebbe09" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,m" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b1c1e3f2-9f26-5edd-a5f3-733721f9597a" :answer/id #uuid "b1c1e3f2-9f26-5edd-a5f3-733721f9597a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.5\\,m" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5aaac2d6-73c4-586e-b4eb-5b146e7bc4a7" :answer/id #uuid "5aaac2d6-73c4-586e-b4eb-5b146e7bc4a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\,m" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d3d50606-3008-5ec2-9486-4aa0714bad59" :answer/id #uuid "d3d50606-3008-5ec2-9486-4aa0714bad59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4.5\\,m" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c378fc4c-4720-5991-98f2-269c5c81ef42" :answer/id #uuid "c378fc4c-4720-5991-98f2-269c5c81ef42" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\,m" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1eab4807-9d88-5a37-9ff9-fc1404b92d43" :question/id #uuid "1eab4807-9d88-5a37-9ff9-fc1404b92d43" :question/math-academy-id "q-163804" :question/problem "![](images/62/6267809d1cc251384417967147434e9d44f4caf9e5fb0de1f10b0291952f75cf.png)\n\nTwo point masses $A$ and $B$ are connected by a rigid, massless rod of length $8\\,yd$ that is perfectly balanced on a fulcrum, as shown above. If $A$ has mass $3\\,lb$ and is $6\\,yd$ from the fulcrum, find the mass of $B.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $m$ be the mass of $B.$\nThe length of the rod is $8\\,yd$ and the distance between the fulcrum and $A$ is $6\\,yd.$ So, the distance between the fulcrum and $B$ is\n\n$$\n8-6=2\\,yd,\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/f3/f3efa18d3ae4e9a7f23f805dd314b9d04f50bb03ec3ead20a82a8e4c586e96a7.png)\n\nLet's write down the moment of each mass about the fulcrum:\n\n- The moment of mass $A$ equals $-3\\cdot 6=-18\\,\\text{lb}\\cdot \\text{yd}$ (negative since the motion induced by this mass would be counterclockwise).\n\n- The moment of mass $B$ equals $m\\cdot 2=2m\\,\\text{lb}\\cdot \\text{yd}$ (positive since the motion induced by this mass would be clockwise).\n\nThe *principle of moments* tells us that for the two masses to balance perfectly, the sum of the moments must equal zero.\n\nTherefore, in this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-18+2m & =0 \\\\ 2m & =18 \\\\ m & =9\\,lb.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b58947dd-0890-5213-825b-acc2492cc94c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b58947dd-0890-5213-825b-acc2492cc94c" :answer-field/id #uuid "b58947dd-0890-5213-825b-acc2492cc94c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-83387c3a-60a5-59d9-a8c2-10bf6fe7e9ea" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d046d557-4efa-53b2-a160-e5cc8fdc4cc6" "answer-cc08aec1-617f-57ac-a4d2-d7d539c7bbc2" "answer-d535efaf-9252-579b-aa64-32b9539d84f3" "answer-2d75bc8f-1386-538b-884c-c82c1b411de8" "answer-83387c3a-60a5-59d9-a8c2-10bf6fe7e9ea"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d046d557-4efa-53b2-a160-e5cc8fdc4cc6" :answer/id #uuid "d046d557-4efa-53b2-a160-e5cc8fdc4cc6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10\\,lb" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cc08aec1-617f-57ac-a4d2-d7d539c7bbc2" :answer/id #uuid "cc08aec1-617f-57ac-a4d2-d7d539c7bbc2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8.3\\,lb" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d535efaf-9252-579b-aa64-32b9539d84f3" :answer/id #uuid "d535efaf-9252-579b-aa64-32b9539d84f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8.5\\,lb" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2d75bc8f-1386-538b-884c-c82c1b411de8" :answer/id #uuid "2d75bc8f-1386-538b-884c-c82c1b411de8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\,lb" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-83387c3a-60a5-59d9-a8c2-10bf6fe7e9ea" :answer/id #uuid "83387c3a-60a5-59d9-a8c2-10bf6fe7e9ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9\\,lb" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c47fff30-dc4f-5860-a5ab-d77dfee6da24" :question/id #uuid "c47fff30-dc4f-5860-a5ab-d77dfee6da24" :question/math-academy-id "q-163799" :question/problem "![](images/88/88a0ceeb1f98bd909ebc6eda2c5232075b6f93d4a158ae1ed1cb4943ab08424c.png)\n\nTwo point masses $A$ and $B$ of mass $12\\,lb$ and $15lb$, respectively, are connected by a rigid, massless rod that is perfectly balanced on a fulcrum, as shown above. If the distance between the fulcrum and $B$ is $4\\,yd,$ find the distance between the fulcrum and $A.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $d$ be the distance between the fulcrum and $A,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/ee/eeaf2a4fbefd3066d28fab6b52cbea58f5adac5cd35887ad012691c9847f5caa.png)\n\nLet's write down the moment of each mass about the fulcrum:\n\n- The moment of mass $A$ equals $-12\\cdot d=-12d\\,\\text{lb}\\cdot \\text{yd}$ (negative since the motion induced by this mass would be counterclockwise).\n\n- The moment of mass $B$ equals $15\\cdot 4=60\\,\\text{lb}\\cdot \\text{yd}$ (positive since the motion induced by this mass would be clockwise).\n\nThe *principle of moments* tells us that for the two masses to perfectly balance, the sum of the moments must equal zero.\n\nTherefore, in this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}60-12d & =0 \\\\ 12d & =60 \\\\ d & =5\\,yd.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cac64b06-3b12-5c5c-a8bc-30473739089c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cac64b06-3b12-5c5c-a8bc-30473739089c" :answer-field/id #uuid "cac64b06-3b12-5c5c-a8bc-30473739089c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f1ab0a47-e61f-591a-99b7-e3a76116c65c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5a0cf625-4841-5456-a97f-8120310520d8" "answer-9839f8b7-6fc0-54e7-a873-e1a499914c0b" "answer-f1ab0a47-e61f-591a-99b7-e3a76116c65c" "answer-bafe1ad5-510f-5ebe-8148-58b4f080df6a" "answer-ba147ba9-7721-52fd-a4b9-2bbb7b663fac"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5a0cf625-4841-5456-a97f-8120310520d8" :answer/id #uuid "5a0cf625-4841-5456-a97f-8120310520d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4.5\\,yd" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9839f8b7-6fc0-54e7-a873-e1a499914c0b" :answer/id #uuid "9839f8b7-6fc0-54e7-a873-e1a499914c0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5.5\\,yd" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f1ab0a47-e61f-591a-99b7-e3a76116c65c" :answer/id #uuid "f1ab0a47-e61f-591a-99b7-e3a76116c65c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\,yd" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bafe1ad5-510f-5ebe-8148-58b4f080df6a" :answer/id #uuid "bafe1ad5-510f-5ebe-8148-58b4f080df6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\,yd" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ba147ba9-7721-52fd-a4b9-2bbb7b663fac" :answer/id #uuid "ba147ba9-7721-52fd-a4b9-2bbb7b663fac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7\\,yd" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-77273bb6-e09c-5d72-b951-ab16051ede43" :question/id #uuid "77273bb6-e09c-5d72-b951-ab16051ede43" :question/math-academy-id "q-163801" :question/problem "![](images/4b/4bd2a8d5a2bdb2400646031be209e9bdf8ffaf985c9f5f9672ec1709a8e9947f.png)\n\nTwo point masses $A$ and $B$ of mass $5\\,lb$ and $6lb$, respectively, are connected by a rigid, massless rod that is perfectly balanced on a fulcrum, as shown above. If the distance between the fulcrum and $A$ is $6\\,ft,$ find the distance between the fulcrum and $B.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $d$ be the distance between the fulcrum and $B,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/cb/cbde3ab8e8ebbeae51a4840bf69d729f1bdbe310ac798d378d59290cd9d4f5c7.png)\n\nLet's write down the moment of each mass about the fulcrum:\n\n- The moment of mass $A$ equals $-5\\cdot 6=-30\\,\\text{lb}\\cdot \\text{ft}$ (negative since the motion induced by this mass would be counterclockwise).\n\n- The moment of mass $B$ equals $6\\cdot d=6d\\,\\text{lb}\\cdot \\text{ft}$ (positive since the motion induced by this mass would be clockwise).\n\nThe *principle of moments* tells us that for the two masses to perfectly balance, the sum of the moments must equal zero.\n\nTherefore, in this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6d-30 & =0 \\\\ 6d & =30 \\\\ d & =5\\,ft.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5d4f95eb-e3f0-520b-9c8f-582ca4418684"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5d4f95eb-e3f0-520b-9c8f-582ca4418684" :answer-field/id #uuid "5d4f95eb-e3f0-520b-9c8f-582ca4418684" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e9bfe1d6-81a1-5ef2-8d4f-047a966e8803" :answer-field/choices ["answer-538bbae4-4700-548f-9e79-aa4a944ce842" "answer-5e2db18f-e828-5217-9bb3-5f4e673a8911" "answer-46cbef3b-c8b9-52f5-a9fb-11f5af3fb71c" "answer-034f97fb-7333-50ac-b55a-b30263f8397f" "answer-e9bfe1d6-81a1-5ef2-8d4f-047a966e8803"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-538bbae4-4700-548f-9e79-aa4a944ce842" :answer/id #uuid "538bbae4-4700-548f-9e79-aa4a944ce842" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.5\\,ft" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5e2db18f-e828-5217-9bb3-5f4e673a8911" :answer/id #uuid "5e2db18f-e828-5217-9bb3-5f4e673a8911" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4.5\\,ft" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-46cbef3b-c8b9-52f5-a9fb-11f5af3fb71c" :answer/id #uuid "46cbef3b-c8b9-52f5-a9fb-11f5af3fb71c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\,ft" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-034f97fb-7333-50ac-b55a-b30263f8397f" :answer/id #uuid "034f97fb-7333-50ac-b55a-b30263f8397f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5.5\\,ft" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e9bfe1d6-81a1-5ef2-8d4f-047a966e8803" :answer/id #uuid "e9bfe1d6-81a1-5ef2-8d4f-047a966e8803" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\,ft" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-47a5c5c7-d82d-5d72-883d-d0468b52660c" :question/id #uuid "47a5c5c7-d82d-5d72-883d-d0468b52660c" :question/math-academy-id "q-163832" :question/problem "![](images/0f/0fcb0a0dd58506c39c038cb55b702ae965251dab55f5db477b0f0f6d275240f9.png)\n\nTwo point masses $A$ and $B$ of mass $3\\,lb$ and $5\\,lb$, respectively, are connected by a rigid, massless rod of length $8\\,yd$ that is perfectly balanced on a fulcrum, as shown above. Find the distance between the fulcrum and $A.$" :question/worked-solution "Let ${d}_{1}$ and ${d}_{2}$ be the distances between the fulcrum and $A$ and $B$, respectively, as shown below.\n\n![](images/80/800da868d66524a7970a2ee421af15f64ca0b8019b4c0572209c183245e4cce7.png)\n\nLet's write down the moment of each mass about the fulcrum:\n\n- The moment of mass $A$ equals $-3\\cdot {d}_{1}=-3{d}_{1}\\,\\text{lb}\\cdot \\text{yd}$ (negative since the motion induced by this mass would be counterclockwise).\n\n- The moment of mass $B$ equals $5\\cdot {d}_{2}=5{d}_{2}\\,\\text{lb}\\cdot \\text{yd}$ (positive since the motion induced by this mass would be clockwise).\n\nThe principle of moments tells us that for the two masses to balance perfectly, the sum of the moments must equal zero. \n\nSo, in this case, we have\n\n$$\n5{d}_{2}-3{d}_{1}=0.\n$$\n\nWe need to find ${d}_{1},$ so we eliminate ${d}_{2}.$\nUsing the fact that the rod has length $8\\,yd,$ we have \n\n$$\n{d}_{1}+{d}_{2}=8\\,⟹\\,{d}_{2}=8-{d}_{1}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(8-{d}_{1})-3{d}_{1} & =0 \\\\ 40-5{d}_{1}-3{d}_{1} & =0 \\\\ 8{d}_{1} & =40 \\\\ {d}_{1} & =5\\,yd.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-69b1abfa-706e-5852-a5c3-b3e7382e87de"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-69b1abfa-706e-5852-a5c3-b3e7382e87de" :answer-field/id #uuid "69b1abfa-706e-5852-a5c3-b3e7382e87de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-03e13f43-26d6-5f79-aa7f-0bc2caf7fc91" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cbbfbb39-5af0-5850-aa5a-35f68e541afa" "answer-429ef200-ce65-58de-b8b4-bb16dfb97052" "answer-523080a2-fd93-5726-a8ae-82de7e9111a3" "answer-e63ab868-e020-51ff-801e-26ed935de918" "answer-03e13f43-26d6-5f79-aa7f-0bc2caf7fc91"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cbbfbb39-5af0-5850-aa5a-35f68e541afa" :answer/id #uuid "cbbfbb39-5af0-5850-aa5a-35f68e541afa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\,yd" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-429ef200-ce65-58de-b8b4-bb16dfb97052" :answer/id #uuid "429ef200-ce65-58de-b8b4-bb16dfb97052" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4.8\\,yd" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-523080a2-fd93-5726-a8ae-82de7e9111a3" :answer/id #uuid "523080a2-fd93-5726-a8ae-82de7e9111a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\,yd" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e63ab868-e020-51ff-801e-26ed935de918" :answer/id #uuid "e63ab868-e020-51ff-801e-26ed935de918" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5.5\\,yd" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-03e13f43-26d6-5f79-aa7f-0bc2caf7fc91" :answer/id #uuid "03e13f43-26d6-5f79-aa7f-0bc2caf7fc91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\,yd" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129540 :question/worked-solution "The moment about the origin $O$ of a collection of masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =5, & \\,{m}_{2} & =1, & \\,{m}_{3} & =4, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =2, & \\,{x}_{2} & =3, & \\,{x}_{3} & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate the total moment of this system about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =5\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 3+4\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =10+3+20 \\\\  & =33\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the total moment of the system is $33\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-34792fb0-e735-52af-a0ef-039163fa5c31"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-34792fb0-e735-52af-a0ef-039163fa5c31" :answer-field/id #uuid "34792fb0-e735-52af-a0ef-039163fa5c31" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a99ef063-9bb4-5a90-adf3-9824d7cfd88e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-03a4aef6-25be-5110-bd50-95a6fe6ab732" "answer-a99ef063-9bb4-5a90-adf3-9824d7cfd88e" "answer-f5fc4d5f-8b23-5fce-9333-221e2d1e5669" "answer-434fab85-9e82-54ee-828c-bd4ebc9487ef" "answer-288df93d-6483-5d8b-a67c-5ae837199f5c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-03a4aef6-25be-5110-bd50-95a6fe6ab732" :answer/id #uuid "03a4aef6-25be-5110-bd50-95a6fe6ab732" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a99ef063-9bb4-5a90-adf3-9824d7cfd88e" :answer/id #uuid "a99ef063-9bb4-5a90-adf3-9824d7cfd88e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "33\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f5fc4d5f-8b23-5fce-9333-221e2d1e5669" :answer/id #uuid "f5fc4d5f-8b23-5fce-9333-221e2d1e5669" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "38\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-434fab85-9e82-54ee-828c-bd4ebc9487ef" :answer/id #uuid "434fab85-9e82-54ee-828c-bd4ebc9487ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "42\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-288df93d-6483-5d8b-a67c-5ae837199f5c" :answer/id #uuid "288df93d-6483-5d8b-a67c-5ae837199f5c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b9628c5b-7fa0-5045-9ac2-ad280b61b082" :question/id #uuid "b9628c5b-7fa0-5045-9ac2-ad280b61b082" :question/math-academy-id "q-163192" :question/problem "Consider the collection of point masses ${m}_{1}=3\\,\\text{kg},$ ${m}_{2}=1.5\\,\\text{kg},$ ${m}_{3}=3\\,\\text{kg},$ and ${m}_{4}=5\\,\\text{kg}$ located at ${x}_{1}=-3\\,\\text{m},$ ${x}_{2}=-2\\,\\text{m},$ ${x}_{3}=4\\,\\text{m},$ and ${x}_{4}=6\\,\\text{m},$ respectively, along the $x$-axis. Find the total moment of this system about the origin." :question/worked-solution "The moment about the origin $O$ of a collection of masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =3, & \\,{m}_{2} & =1.5, & \\,{m}_{3} & =3, & \\,{m}_{4} & =5, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-3, & \\,{x}_{2} & =-2, & \\,{x}_{3} & =4, & \\,{x}_{4} & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate the total moment of this system about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3}+{m}_{4}{x}_{4} \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-3)+1.5\\cdot (-2)+3\\cdot 4+5\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =-9-3+12+30 \\\\  & =30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the total moment of the system is $30\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cddb08a9-5244-5687-90c6-ad97b11f840e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cddb08a9-5244-5687-90c6-ad97b11f840e" :answer-field/id #uuid "cddb08a9-5244-5687-90c6-ad97b11f840e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2749f919-671d-5108-8480-233e0187fac6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-74d71cf9-ef7d-5883-ad63-c30ca76ed82e" "answer-2749f919-671d-5108-8480-233e0187fac6" "answer-d31b428a-2604-5abe-80eb-3aeb55ca0cf3" "answer-71369790-e2fa-50aa-9327-d15459bbfc51" "answer-e01064a9-7a92-5391-9b3a-fc20ca374f0b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-74d71cf9-ef7d-5883-ad63-c30ca76ed82e" :answer/id #uuid "74d71cf9-ef7d-5883-ad63-c30ca76ed82e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "27\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2749f919-671d-5108-8480-233e0187fac6" :answer/id #uuid "2749f919-671d-5108-8480-233e0187fac6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d31b428a-2604-5abe-80eb-3aeb55ca0cf3" :answer/id #uuid "d31b428a-2604-5abe-80eb-3aeb55ca0cf3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "33\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-71369790-e2fa-50aa-9327-d15459bbfc51" :answer/id #uuid "71369790-e2fa-50aa-9327-d15459bbfc51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "39\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e01064a9-7a92-5391-9b3a-fc20ca374f0b" :answer/id #uuid "e01064a9-7a92-5391-9b3a-fc20ca374f0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "54\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-66bc40ec-8b7f-5a7f-a822-c2240ee2d9f5" :question/id #uuid "66bc40ec-8b7f-5a7f-a822-c2240ee2d9f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-163227" :question/problem "![](images/8f/8fa845de716b1043248c3fb7d185e241d3d89688b185901b4b8275a6c89368f3.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses shown above, where the distances along the $x$-axis are measured in meters. Find the total moment of this system about the origin." :question/worked-solution "The moment about the origin $O$ of a collection of masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =2, & \\,{m}_{2} & =2, & \\,{m}_{3} & =1.5, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-3, & \\,{x}_{2} & =3, & \\,{x}_{3} & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate the total moment of this system about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-3)+2\\cdot 3+1.5\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-6+6+6 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the total moment of the system is $6\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-97b0e30b-489b-5dcc-b571-b64fdb48fdeb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-97b0e30b-489b-5dcc-b571-b64fdb48fdeb" :answer-field/id #uuid "97b0e30b-489b-5dcc-b571-b64fdb48fdeb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e32a3a60-7d0b-5729-b7b2-7f24e34d271f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0ac4ada0-f0a3-5031-b133-f63a29de5e46" "answer-d8b16c3d-e750-582e-9fe3-5bb188fdac5b" "answer-a8a10a6b-0669-5203-a65a-369a6a997989" "answer-e95b2fca-3c87-59da-b304-224750f23202" "answer-e32a3a60-7d0b-5729-b7b2-7f24e34d271f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0ac4ada0-f0a3-5031-b133-f63a29de5e46" :answer/id #uuid "0ac4ada0-f0a3-5031-b133-f63a29de5e46" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d8b16c3d-e750-582e-9fe3-5bb188fdac5b" :answer/id #uuid "d8b16c3d-e750-582e-9fe3-5bb188fdac5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a8a10a6b-0669-5203-a65a-369a6a997989" :answer/id #uuid "a8a10a6b-0669-5203-a65a-369a6a997989" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e95b2fca-3c87-59da-b304-224750f23202" :answer/id #uuid "e95b2fca-3c87-59da-b304-224750f23202" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e32a3a60-7d0b-5729-b7b2-7f24e34d271f" :answer/id #uuid "e32a3a60-7d0b-5729-b7b2-7f24e34d271f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129539 :question/problem "Consider the collection of point masses ${m}_{1}=0.5\\,\\text{kg},$ ${m}_{2}=2\\,\\text{kg},$ and ${m}_{3}=1\\,\\text{kg}$ located at ${x}_{1}=2\\,\\text{m},$ ${x}_{2}=3\\,\\text{m},$ and ${x}_{3}=5\\,\\text{m},$ respectively, along the $x$-axis. Find the total moment of this system about the origin." :question/worked-solution "The moment about the origin $O$ of a collection of masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =0.5, & \\,{m}_{2} & =2, & \\,{m}_{3} & =1, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =2, & \\,{x}_{2} & =3, & \\,{x}_{3} & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate the total moment of this system about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =0.5\\cdot 2+2\\cdot 3+1\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =1+6+5 \\\\  & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the total moment of the system is $12\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-95d601b6-4069-5e2c-a253-cae39d9d2f73"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-95d601b6-4069-5e2c-a253-cae39d9d2f73" :answer-field/id #uuid "95d601b6-4069-5e2c-a253-cae39d9d2f73" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-438a0eed-2e4d-52ed-8a38-78337ec5f7d6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-425b22e4-8fcb-5dfd-928d-1d2db5b318ae" "answer-438a0eed-2e4d-52ed-8a38-78337ec5f7d6" "answer-255800d9-1133-5a68-aa65-dbf3bde73548" "answer-6dd89118-eabd-5dbf-ad93-a188fc17bf8d" "answer-62277929-a5ce-5bd8-8467-0e5ddaa918e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-425b22e4-8fcb-5dfd-928d-1d2db5b318ae" :answer/id #uuid "425b22e4-8fcb-5dfd-928d-1d2db5b318ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-438a0eed-2e4d-52ed-8a38-78337ec5f7d6" :answer/id #uuid "438a0eed-2e4d-52ed-8a38-78337ec5f7d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-255800d9-1133-5a68-aa65-dbf3bde73548" :answer/id #uuid "255800d9-1133-5a68-aa65-dbf3bde73548" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6dd89118-eabd-5dbf-ad93-a188fc17bf8d" :answer/id #uuid "6dd89118-eabd-5dbf-ad93-a188fc17bf8d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-62277929-a5ce-5bd8-8467-0e5ddaa918e6" :answer/id #uuid "62277929-a5ce-5bd8-8467-0e5ddaa918e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d3c48087-507b-57b2-8663-35cf3ca6e4b3" :question/id #uuid "d3c48087-507b-57b2-8663-35cf3ca6e4b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-163191" :question/problem "Consider the collection of point masses ${m}_{1}=5\\,\\text{kg},$ ${m}_{2}=4\\,\\text{kg},$ and ${m}_{3}=2.5\\,\\text{kg}$ located at ${x}_{1}=-1\\,\\text{m},$ ${x}_{2}=1\\,\\text{m},$ and ${x}_{3}=6\\,\\text{m},$ respectively, along the $x$-axis. Find the total moment of this system about the origin." :question/worked-solution "The moment about the origin $O$ of a collection of masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =5, & \\,{m}_{2} & =4, & \\,{m}_{3} & =2.5, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-1, & \\,{x}_{2} & =1, & \\,{x}_{3} & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate the total moment of this system about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =5\\cdot (-1)+4\\cdot 1+2.5\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =-5+4+15 \\\\  & =14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the total moment of the system is $14\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f6ce2973-a27d-54ac-a874-d3afed02d1eb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f6ce2973-a27d-54ac-a874-d3afed02d1eb" :answer-field/id #uuid "f6ce2973-a27d-54ac-a874-d3afed02d1eb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f809735f-34d2-5813-9672-5b25d618bbc0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c840e2a6-932d-5fdb-9ae8-909cd22ba477" "answer-9e31a054-d2a3-5270-9722-0e93e5caf15b" "answer-f809735f-34d2-5813-9672-5b25d618bbc0" "answer-fee4510b-cee5-5419-893d-8433522a711d" "answer-db84e61d-b052-5da1-8494-93d338ab4cc1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c840e2a6-932d-5fdb-9ae8-909cd22ba477" :answer/id #uuid "c840e2a6-932d-5fdb-9ae8-909cd22ba477" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9e31a054-d2a3-5270-9722-0e93e5caf15b" :answer/id #uuid "9e31a054-d2a3-5270-9722-0e93e5caf15b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f809735f-34d2-5813-9672-5b25d618bbc0" :answer/id #uuid "f809735f-34d2-5813-9672-5b25d618bbc0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fee4510b-cee5-5419-893d-8433522a711d" :answer/id #uuid "fee4510b-cee5-5419-893d-8433522a711d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "19\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-db84e61d-b052-5da1-8494-93d338ab4cc1" :answer/id #uuid "db84e61d-b052-5da1-8494-93d338ab4cc1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-cd5d39c2-8301-5260-adfd-2e9f69bcfb7d" :question/id #uuid "cd5d39c2-8301-5260-adfd-2e9f69bcfb7d" :question/math-academy-id "q-163263" :question/problem "![](images/e0/e025510c351042df35e2c077a4179e808e5fac47d9dad3530e2aaa7346818055.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses above, where the $x$-coordinates are measured in meters. What is the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass for this system?" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass, denoted $\\overset{―}{x},$ of a collection of point masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- ${M}_{O}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =3, & \\,{m}_{2} & =2, & \\,{m}_{3} & =5, & \\,{m}_{4} & =6, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-3, & \\,{x}_{2} & =-1.5, & \\,{x}_{3} & =2, & \\,{x}_{4} & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3}+{m}_{4} \\\\  & =3+2+5+6 \\\\  & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the total moment of the system about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3}+{m}_{4}{x}_{4} \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-3)+2\\cdot (-1.5)+5\\cdot 2+6\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-9-3+10+18 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m}=\\frac{16}{16}=1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a6543621-3d2a-5603-91ba-a030e58feb98"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a6543621-3d2a-5603-91ba-a030e58feb98" :answer-field/id #uuid "a6543621-3d2a-5603-91ba-a030e58feb98" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-fea357d6-77b7-5488-bfc4-bb69cc0bd5df" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c364667f-2d2b-5a4c-b45b-c805c408efe2" "answer-9fc5d90a-966c-556a-ab09-8e2c30e34715" "answer-fea357d6-77b7-5488-bfc4-bb69cc0bd5df" "answer-f45ca283-993d-5975-99da-f600e63ae2d9" "answer-1c3f78f7-1faf-5bea-9426-5faedda429c7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c364667f-2d2b-5a4c-b45b-c805c408efe2" :answer/id #uuid "c364667f-2d2b-5a4c-b45b-c805c408efe2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9fc5d90a-966c-556a-ab09-8e2c30e34715" :answer/id #uuid "9fc5d90a-966c-556a-ab09-8e2c30e34715" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fea357d6-77b7-5488-bfc4-bb69cc0bd5df" :answer/id #uuid "fea357d6-77b7-5488-bfc4-bb69cc0bd5df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f45ca283-993d-5975-99da-f600e63ae2d9" :answer/id #uuid "f45ca283-993d-5975-99da-f600e63ae2d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1c3f78f7-1faf-5bea-9426-5faedda429c7" :answer/id #uuid "1c3f78f7-1faf-5bea-9426-5faedda429c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-26263261-ed01-57e5-8398-ad944dae02a2" :question/id #uuid "26263261-ed01-57e5-8398-ad944dae02a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-163264" :question/problem "![](images/17/17b621de27c4ad429c44ce1a91cd254c885ee83e7d97b03410cae64c3fc52284.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses above, where the $x$-coordinates are measured in meters. What is the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass for this system?" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass, denoted $\\overset{―}{x},$ of a collection of point masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- ${M}_{O}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =3, & \\,{m}_{2} & =1, & \\,{m}_{3} & =6, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =1, & \\,{x}_{2} & =3, & \\,{x}_{3} & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3} \\\\  & =3+1+6 \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the total moment of the system about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 3+6\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =3+3+24 \\\\  & =30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m}=\\frac{30}{10}=3.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f4d4aa4f-d888-5e28-9631-466adc355c5f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f4d4aa4f-d888-5e28-9631-466adc355c5f" :answer-field/id #uuid "f4d4aa4f-d888-5e28-9631-466adc355c5f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-307fc3cb-086a-5864-8bcc-9336bcb9a962" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b07549fb-a968-5e5b-9b6f-3f8a0c2caee2" "answer-307fc3cb-086a-5864-8bcc-9336bcb9a962" "answer-f2171a8c-ecd1-53d5-8108-37a442deda8c" "answer-bcc4aeb4-4db4-5d9e-ba2a-6df5b9c8acce" "answer-5aa2c9d7-f510-584d-869a-fe8860620b6d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b07549fb-a968-5e5b-9b6f-3f8a0c2caee2" :answer/id #uuid "b07549fb-a968-5e5b-9b6f-3f8a0c2caee2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-307fc3cb-0